%I A398906 #35 Nov 22 2026 00:37:04
%S A398906 1,3,7,13,21,30,43,57,72,91,111,132,157,183,210,241,273,306,343,381,
%T A398906 420,463,507,552,601,651,702,757,813,870,931,993,1056,1123,1191,1260,
%U A398906 1333,1407,1482,1561,1641,1722,1807,1893,1980,2071,2163,2256,2353,2451,2550
%N A398906 Maximum number of painted tiles in a hexagonal grid of side length n+1 such that no two painted tiles touch and all unpainted tiles form a contiguous area.
%C A398906 Inspired by A239231, with application to a hexagonal grid vs a square.
%C A398906 These might be called "hexagonal Heyawake numbers".
%H A398906 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398906/b398906.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A398906 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heyawake">Heyawake</a>.
%H A398906 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1,1,-2,1).
%F A398906 a(n) = n*(n+1) + k, where:
%F A398906 k=1 when (n mod 3) < 2 or n = 2;
%F A398906 k=0 otherwise.
%F A398906 From _Jianing Song_, Nov 21 2026: (Start)
%F A398906 a(n) = 2*a(n-1) - a(n-2) + a(n-3) - 2*a(n-4) + a(n-5) for n >= 8.
%F A398906 G.f.: (1 + x + 2*x^2 + x^3 + x^4 - x^5 + 2*x^6 - x^7)/((1 - x)^3*(1 + x + x^2)).
%F A398906 E.g.f.: (2/3+2*x+x^2)*exp(x) + (2/3)*exp(-x/2)*sin(sqrt(3)*x/2+Pi/6) + x^2/2. (End)
%e A398906 This sequence is achieved by applying the painting pattern:
%e A398906    O X O
%e A398906   X O O X
%e A398906    O X O
%e A398906 to equal sided hexagonal grids. A grid's shell size (n) is determined by how many cycles of tiles are applied around a central tile.
%e A398906 When applied to a grid with shell size n=5, and the pattern is initially applied to the uppermost left tile, the resulting grid looks like this:
%e A398906        X O O X O O
%e A398906       O O X O O X O
%e A398906      O X O O X O O X
%e A398906     X O O X O O X O O
%e A398906    O O X O O X O O X O
%e A398906   O X O O X O O X O O X
%e A398906    O O X O O X O O X O
%e A398906     X O O X O O X O O
%e A398906      O X O O X O O X
%e A398906       O O X O O X O
%e A398906        X O O X O O
%e A398906 which is 30 painted tiles.
%e A398906 This pattern should be optimal for filling a hexagonal grid with non-contiguous painted tiles, including the special case of n=2, in which painting the center tile and every other tile in its outer shell yields one more painted tile than using this configuration:
%e A398906     O X O
%e A398906    X O O X
%e A398906   O O X O O
%e A398906    X O O X
%e A398906     O X O
%e A398906 This should be the only case where painting the center tile is optimal for shell sizes n where n mod 3 != 0.
%t A398906 A398906[n_] := n^2 + n + Boole[n == 2 || Mod[n, 3] < 2];
%t A398906 Array[A398906, 60, 0] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 20 2026 *)
%o A398906 (PARI) a(n) = n*(n+1)/2 + (n==2 || n%3<2) \\ _Jianing Song_, Nov 21 2026
%K A398906 easy,nonn,new
%O A398906 0,2
%A A398906 _Dan Klein_, Nov 03 2026
%E A398906 Formula simplified by Paolo Xausa.
